course: dictionary
lesson: 4309
title: Words for shopping
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: You will meet words like grocery in shops, on lists and in news stories. Read the words around them to find their meaning. «In Milton Keynes six-wheeled robots deliver groceries» tells you the robots bring something to people, and the things are for the home, so groceries must be food and other things people buy.
explain: Grocery can also describe another word, like an adjective. A grocery store is a shop that sells food, and a grocery list is a list of food to buy. To check a meaning, swap in a word that fits. "Food shop" fits in "grocery store", so your meaning is probably right.
explain: The sentence also gives safety clues: «people should give them space and never climb on them.» Robots on the pavement are for delivering groceries, and they are not for playing on. When you read about shops, look for the words that tell you what people do there and what is kept safe.
fact: A grocery, or grocery store, is a shop that sells food and things for the home.
fact: Groceries are the food and other things you buy there, like milk, bread, fruit and soap.
fact: «Grocery shopping» means going to buy the food for the week.
fact: «Grocery list» uses grocery as an adjective: it is a list of things to buy at the shop.
fact: «Deliver groceries» means bring the shopping to people's homes, like the robots in Milton Keynes.
exercise: What is a grocery store? | A place that fixes cars | A school for cooks | *A shop that sells food and things for the home | A park with bicycles
exercise: «The robot brought the groceries to the door.» What are groceries? | Robots with six wheels | Lists you write at school | *Food and other things you buy at a shop | Bags with holes in them
exercise: Mum writes a grocery list before she goes out. What is a grocery list? | *A list of food and things to buy | A list of the robots' names | A book of recipes for cakes | A list of shops to close
test: Which word means the food and things you buy at a shop? | *Groceries | Sensor | Wheel | Pavement
test: Why should you stay with your grown-up in the grocery store? | So the store closes early | *So you stay safe | So you can climb on the shelves | So you can drive the trolley
exam: In which phrase is grocery used as an adjective, describing another word? | two groceries | *a grocery list | bags of groceries | a grocer's shop
